*.duckdb
*.duckdb.*
bt_*.csv
backtest_*.csv
_btclean.csv
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
duckdb_tmp/
~$*

c?.csv
d?.csv
e?.csv
full*.csv
probe*.csv
*.tmp

# secrets: never commit
access_password.txt
anthropic_key.txt

# large regenerable data artefacts (kept on disk, out of git)
*.joblib
*_by_year.csv
master_backtest*.csv
bt_v3_routes.txt

# runtime state / scratch previews (mutate every run)
entry_counter.txt
*_PREVIEW.html
_synth_*.csv

# added 8 August 2026, from the reconciler's LEAVE list and the tree comparison.
# venv/ carries its own .gitignore containing *, which is why git has never seen it
# and why audit_split.py does not finish. The explicit entries are belt and braces.
venv/
app/venv/
app/avia-forecast/venv/

# computed, regenerable, machine-local: the drive-time cache catchment_master.py
# writes. It belongs to whichever machine did the computing.
_dt_cache/

# back-test master tables: outputs, circa 11MB, regenerable from the stores, and
# read only by the July analysis scripts. master_backtest*.csv is already above.
master_complete*.csv
master_v?_complete*.csv

# result dumps from the July accuracy runs. The findings are written up in
# BT2_BACKTEST_PROGRAMME.md; these are the raw console output.
*_results_*.txt
_dot_test.csv
_smoke.csv

# Pre-test and diagnostic outputs. app/pretest_qsi.csv, a result file from 3 July, was swept
# into the first commit by git add -A and then shipped down to the workstation in the clone,
# where a watcher waiting for tonight's run to produce it found the stale one already present
# and released early. Results do not belong in the tool repo: they belong with the data.
pretest_*.csv
bt_ab_*/
*_direct.log
run.log

# bt2, the accuracy programme. Code and the experiment log are committed; artifacts and computed
# intermediates are not, because they are 42MB of build output and they belong with the data.
# bt2/README.md records the SHA-256 of every artifact behind a published claim, so a claim can be
# traced to the thing that produced it even though the binary lives elsewhere.
# Set AVIA_BT2_DIR to the data location so runs never write artifacts into the repo.
bt2/*.pkl
bt2/*.json
!bt2/ddfs_packs/
bt2/*.csv
bt2/__pycache__/

# machine config: the deck renderer's local paths. avia_config.example.json IS committed
# as the template; the resolved copy never is, per point 4 of the tool standard.
avia_config.json

# generated decks and workbooks. Outputs belong in the output folder, not the repo.
# Already-tracked .pptx files at the root and in app/ stay tracked until they are
# deliberately removed; this stops new ones arriving by accident.
*.pptx
*.pdf

# NOT ignored, deliberately, so the decision is visible:
#   app_avia_style/          already tracked, 8 files. The frozen rollback copy is a
#                            record. Removing it is a separate decision, not a side
#                            effect of a .gitignore edit.
#   _archive_old_versions/   holds calibration_library_v7, __6_ and
#                            research_to_presentation. Already tracked, and it is the
#                            record of what came before.
#   accuracy_dist.json       an INPUT: methodology_page.py reads it, and it going
#                            missing from one tree is what left the proof card with no
#                            distribution to draw on 7 August.
#   the July scratch (runner*, score*, bench*, importance*, subgroups*,
#   explore_segments, stage_runner): these go to app/attic/ and are COMMITTED there in
#   a second commit. An attic folder that is committed is a record; a file ignored is a
#   file that exists on one machine only, which is the fault this repo exists to end.
